+    "There exists some specific permutation of the summands that will generate any given result when the sum is conditionally convergent.  A sum over some series $a_n$ is conditionally convergent if $\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty |a_n| = \\infty$.  Returning to electrostatics, we introduce the integral analog of the potential expression above, avoiding the singularity by neglecting the infinitesimal point $\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{0}$:\n",
